From 038f29b9e254621a80400b4df414343b97a84b98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mtk-ccci: NetAgent for the PDNs the modem brings up itself
 (IMS)

The modem brings some PDNs up by itself, the IMS one among them, and
reports each with +EIF: <id>, ifup, <type>, <address>. Do what the stock
NetAgent and netd do for them: bring the ccmni up with the network's
IPv6 interface identifier, router advertisements for its prefix but no
default route, confirm it (AT+EIF=<id>, "ifst", "up"), report the
global address SLAAC gives it (AT+EIF=<id>, "ipupdate", 2, ...), add the
IPv4 address of a later +EIF: ifchg, take it down on ifdown, and confirm
the IMS manager's bearer requests (+EIMSPDN: "notify" -> AT+EIMSPDN=
"confirm", <aid>, 0) as the stock RIL does when nothing above it
listens. Without these the IMS PDN never finished coming up and IMS
never registered.

A data bearer's PDN still comes up in its +EAPNACT reply. The NetAgent's
ifup handler is held during the activation, and the bearer now tells its
own +EIF: ifup from one the modem brought up meanwhile by the address
+EPDN reports for its PDN, handing the other to the NetAgent; it confirms
its interface once identified.

The modem's IMS controller turns off with the radio, and the stock RIL
sends the IMS configuration again whenever the radio comes on: after
powering up, send AT+EIMSCFG with the device's ID_MM_MTK_CCCI_IMS_CFG.
